/Title (Explanation: The outer function declares the variable count. The inner function accesses and modifies it. The outer function returns the inner function, and the returned function continues to remember the value of count between calls. Advantages: Closures help with data privacy, preserve state between function calls, create private variables, and are useful in callbacks and event handlers.)
